ons concentrate variation in fewer directions than item embeddings, particularly for Industrial_and_Scientific and Electronics.\",\n    \"Training branch allocation remains unknown: approximately 19–20% terminal-position coverage describes the diagnostic loader only.\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence\": {\n    \"headline_metrics\": {\n      \"Electronics:pos_neg_margin_p10\": 0.6623,\n      \"Movies_and_TV:pos_neg_margin_p10\": 2.8445,\n      \"Industrial_and_Scientific:appended_mask_users_rankme\": 24.3300,\n      \"Industrial_and_Scientific:real_items_rankme\": 49.6040\n    },\n    \"brief_metric_read\": {\n      \"pos_neg_margin_p10\": \"Lower-tail separation remains positive, but Electronics has less margin.\",\n      \"representation_geometry\": \"Nonzero centered variance and substantial effective ranks argue against complete collapse.\",\n      \"training_branch_allocation\": \"Null for all categories; actual training allocation is unavailable.\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n    ",
